<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!--
      The launch splash's mark, in exactly ONE place because two frames have to
      agree on it: @drawable/splash_background draws it before this process has
      composed anything, and LaunchSplash draws it again as soon as Compose
      takes over. A size that differed between them is a logo that jumps at the
      handoff - the one thing the two halves exist to prevent.

      160dp is the launcher vector's own 108dp tile scaled up. The mark inside
      that tile is 62 of its 108 units, so the brass button reads at ~92dp:
      about a fifth of a 540dp-tall TV, with the tile's built-in padding left
      as the breathing room around it.
    -->
    <dimen name="splash_logo_size">160dp</dimen>
</resources>
